		{"id":"530c9d7444377c06","type":"text","text":"# **New Homework** \n### - **Memorize watching strategies**\n### - **Theme Words B: At the doctor's.**","x":-1514,"y":-1228,"width":650,"height":172,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"2a24b467cd64d152","type":"text","text":"\n## **08:15** -\tWhats in Chapter 2 \n## **08:25** - Watching A  **Exercises 5-9**\n## **08:40** - Reading \n","x":-1513,"y":-1423,"width":649,"height":156,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"43f7895bc24e2e7e","type":"text","text":"# **Today's Class: Starting Chapter 2 **","x":-1490,"y":-1524,"width":602,"height":68,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"2ac4386465b9b020","x":-562,"y":-1524,"width":556,"height":739,"color":"3","type":"text","text":"### Watching Strategies\n\n| Strategy                     | Explanation                                                          | Example                                                |\n| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **1. Predicting**            | Before watching, predict what the video will be about.               | Look at the title or first image. What do you expect?  |\n| **2. Watching for gist**     | Focus on the general meaning rather than every word.                 | What is the video mainly about?                        |\n| **3. Watching for details**  | Look and listen for specific information.                            | Where does the conversation take place?                |\n| **4. Using visual clues**    | Pay attention to facial expressions, gestures and surroundings.      | How can you tell someone is frightened?                |\n| **5. Guessing from context** | Use what you see and hear to understand unfamiliar words.            | What might an unfamiliar word mean in this situation?  |\n| **6. Making inferences**     | Understand information that is not directly stated.                  | Why do you think the person is lying?                  |\n| **7. Identifying key words** | Focus on important words instead of trying to understand everything. | Which three words helped you understand the situation? |\n| **8. Checking predictions**  | Compare your original predictions with what actually happens.        | Was your prediction correct? What changed your mind?   |\n\n"}
	],
